    "detail": "A role system first. An access row now carries what that person may open: which heads they work with, and which of eleven areas are switched off. It is a deny list, so a business that never opens the screen behaves exactly as it does now and anything shipped later is available to everybody rather than invisible until every member is edited. Heads are named instead, because \"only these two\" is what people mean. Administrators are never restricted by it, since they can lift any of it in a click.\n\nEnforced on the server, not only hidden: every write goes through one batch endpoint that names its table, so one check covers each area, and a conversation with a head somebody was not given cannot be saved at all. The calendar, briefings and the inbox check for themselves. The inbox checks both ways, so nobody fills a mailbox that cannot be opened. It is not an isolation boundary and the module says so: the workspace still loads as one document, and anybody who must not see a thing belongs in their own workspace.\n\nNeeds drizzle/0011_member_permissions.sql.\n\nThen the rest of the list:\n\nThe composer buttons sat low on a phone. The attach buttons carried a touch target and grew to 48px there while the field and the send button stayed 40, so the row took its height from the tallest and everything else hung off the bottom of it. All three are one line tall now, measured at dead centre in both pointer modes.\n\nConversation titles read like English. The old one harvested words and joined them, so \"I need pricing for websites to sell\" filed itself as \"Pricing Websites Sell\": every word was in the message and the phrase was not. It keeps the sentence now, and once the first reply is in, a cheap model reads both sides and names the subject properly on the business's own key.\n\nAn operator opening their own business got the whole deployment's reports under their own company name, and running a pass from there swept every customer. Reports are asked for by scope now.\n\nYour people, Briefings and Integrations had no scroll container, so anything past the fold was simply unreachable. The usage table had no padding between columns, so eight of them shared edges. The top bar carried a second menu button and a second search. The dashboard stacked its two actions on a phone. Reports and feedback can be deleted by the operator. The model line is gone from the head profile, where the footer under every answer already said it. And the copy is labels rather than sentences again in the places it had crept back: Dismiss and Reviewed rather than Not a problem and Looked at it.",
