    "detail": "The sign-in page is public, and it printed the allowlist: with a single approved address it rendered that address in full, which was the case for the whole time only one account existed. Anyone who found the URL was handed the exact address to aim a phishing attempt at, on a page that also tells them the workspace uses Google.\n\nNeither the addresses nor the count now. Someone who is meant to have access already knows which account to use, and someone who is not learns nothing. The rejection message tells a new colleague what to do about it instead of stating a fact they cannot act on.",
