    "date": "2026-08-31",
    "title": "Add an onboarding page to send people on their first day",
    "detail": "One page rather than a wizard, because it is meant to be linked, skimmed, and come back to. It reads the workspace rather than hardcoding it, so it names the actual heads and their count and stays right when either changes.\n\nFour parts: what this is, how to get something useful out of it, what the rest of the app is for, and what not to do. That last part is the reason it exists. No secrets in a conversation, no answer treated as checked, no mistaking Legal or Finance for professionals, no assuming it is private given an administrator can review it, and nothing published unread.\n\nBehind sign-in like everything else, which costs nothing here: the sign-in page carries a from parameter, so the link lands on this page once they authenticate. Anyone who cannot sign in has no use for the instructions.",
