    "detail": "Two measured problems, both found by testing rather than reading.\n\nThe store's context memo listed seven derived lists as dependencies, each written as `remote?.x ?? []`. While a source was still undefined that fallback minted a fresh array every render, so the dependencies changed every render, so the memo rebuilt the context value every render, so every component reading the store re-rendered with it. The memo was pure cost. One frozen shared empty array fixes it. The same review caught projectList missing from that dependency array outright, which meant a project created in local mode did not appear until something unrelated changed.\n\nThe sign-in page was pulling 213KB gzipped, IndexedDB included, to render one button, because StoreProvider and AppShell sat in the root layout and wrapped a page shown to people who are not signed in. Moving them into an (app) route group takes it to 148KB, measured over the network before and after. Route groups do not appear in URLs, and all 25 routes build unchanged.\n\nAlso: eslint, which is how the dependency bug surfaced, with exhaustive-deps raised to an error and wired into CI alongside the guard tests. upgrade-insecure-requests is gone from the CSP, having broken a production build served over http while protecting against mixed content the policy already forbids. And /api/workspace/status is out of the proxy matcher, since answering \"you are not signed in\" is its whole job and redirecting it made the store parse the sign-in page as JSON.",
